    "mainIdea": {
      "text": "When the remote rope of Arendelle’s North Mountain warning bell broke, Anna, Elsa, Ms. Lin, and student 2 had to cross an echoing snow bridge before a blizzard arrived. The bridge turned spoken directions into real paths, so their conflicting commands split the road and trapped them at its center. Elsa discovered that magic could protect their footing but could not choose the correct way. Ms. Lin asked everyone to report observations in turn, and student 2 confirmed the tower’s position. After the group agreed on one instruction, the bridge formed a safe route, which Elsa supported. At the tower, they followed another shared plan: Elsa freed and steadied the hammer, Anna and Ms. Lin pulled together, and 2 chose the right moment. Their united action warned Arendelle in time."
    },
